  "findings": [
    "The conditional helper rewrites the exact parent coefficient at softParentEdge j g and the exact core coefficient at g using canonical treeCoefficient_farOnly over ℚ. This theorem identifies the complete full-interval output of the actual geometric open sums; it does not identify individual auxiliary open sums.",
    "The consumed farOnlyOutput_duplication theorem uses the actual ordinary inverse and covers every distinguished position for a core with n≥3. Its full endpoint cases include s=0 and s=n−1, and its near arrays are removed separately on parent and core by the complete-output factorization. No root independence or wall law is invoked by this specialization.",
    "The far array in hpull is precisely geometricBoundaryArray of softInsertion P j q epsilon at the actual root, equated to tripleLift at the actual softRootPosition. The first theorem honestly exposes this intermediate condition; the uniform theorem obtains it from soft_geometric_duplication_data instead of keeping it as an extra final hypothesis.",
